From: DongDongJu <commisori28@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:40:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Fix native replay startup with an optional subscription
 handshake

A replay snapshot can complete before a late native SUB has installed its
filter, losing batches between replay and live delivery. Add an opt-in nonce
challenge on the existing ROUTER and XPUB sockets. The client subscribes to
its unique nonce only after receiving the challenge; observing that filter
proves the earlier native topic filter is installed on the same connection.
Serve the existing replay bytes and END marker only after this proof.

READY carries a stable random publisher incarnation so a persistent observer
can distinguish reconnects from engine restarts without guessing from clocks
or native sequence numbers. Pending challenges are bounded and expire.
Default PUB and legacy replay behavior remain unchanged.

Validate real TCP delayed consumers, duplicate ordinary subscriptions,
cancellation capacity/expiry, exact CPU replay/live bytes, and configuration.
The combined native publisher and observer suite passes 27 tests and 28
subtests without GPUs. Use a scoped context in the existing port reservation
test so asynchronous ZeroMQ close cannot race the publisher bind.

